            <ArticleTitle>Is traveler's diarrhea a significant risk factor for the development of irritable bowel syndrome? A prospective study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>898-901</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A total of 564 travelers were enrolled in a study aimed at investigating the influence of traveler's diarrhea in the development of irritable bowel syndrome. At 6-7 months after repatriation, we found that an episode of traveler's diarrhea was associated with a quintuple risk of developing irritable bowel syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
